Hello,

here is a small patch that simplifies the untrapping of boxes.

If the option confirm_untrap is set then the game acts just like it does 
normally. But if confirm_untrap is negated then in one situation there 
is a change:

If you are standing in a postion that has no floor trap and has only one 
box then using the command #untrap (m-u) down (>) does not ask if you 
want check the box for traps but instead just tells you if no trap was 
found or if found asks if you want to disarm it.

The only benefit of this is that the command becomes repeatable if it 
failed to find a trap. So you can repeat the action by ^A.

